From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:47:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] Build fixes for cross-compiling to RISC OS

- configure.ac: the GCCSDK triplet is arm-riscos-gnueabihf (OS field
  "gnueabihf"), so the OS check matches the whole $host; no -lintl/-liconv
  on RISC OS (UnixLib has iconv; NLS is off).
- autorevision is a host tool: link it without configure's cross
  LDFLAGS/LIBS (-static, riscos_output.o), and fix a return type that a
  current host g++ rejects.
- The .l/.y files: the flex version test treated flex 2.6 as older than
  2.5.9; bison 3 dropped YYPARSE_PARAM (use %parse-param and a two-argument
  yyerror).
- exceptionhandler.c: the Unix crash handler (fork + gdb) is off on RISC
  OS; UnixLib prints its own backtrace.
- tex.h, piestate.c, screen.h: includes that SDL 1.2's headers used to
  bring in.
